# A6a R4: `buf[i + k]` with i a loop counter bounded by its loop's test
# (`cultw i, N` whose true edge dominates the access) folds k into the
# symbol (reassoc, testbound): one index, constant offsets. The twin
# reassoc_loop_off pins the index computed for each access.
# the shape pinned here is the text rules' and the slots' own: the X/Y colour
# (lot XY, 2026-11-14) would hold this case's counter or index in a register
# itself (its shapes: xy_colour.checks)
env QBE_NO_XY_COLOUR=1
in fill4: present sta\.l fbuf,x\n\tsta\.l fbuf\+2,x\n\tsta\.l fbuf\+4,x\n\tsta\.l fbuf\+6,x
in fill4: absent asl a
in pairs: present sta\.w nbuf,x\n[^\n]*\n\tsta\.w nbuf\+2,x
in pairs: absent asl a
# a bound the loop's test does not give as a constant: i + 1 may wrap
in open_bound: absent nbuf\+2
in open_bound: present inc a\n\tasl a\n\ttax
